ield had doubled from 20 skiers to 40 in Cortina. The event appeared on the FIS World Championship program in 1954, with Soviet skier " [:a {:href "/athletes/80591"} "Lyubov Kozyreva"] " winning ahead of the Finns " [:a {:href "/athletes/81691"} "Siiri Rantanen"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/81295"} "Mirja Hietamies"] ". Kozyreva had also won the pre-Olympic trial at Cortina in 1955."] "\n\n" [:p {} "No official intermediate times were taken during the event, and the first starter on the Soviet team, " [:a {:href "/athletes/81606"} "Anna Kaaleste"] ", with start number 7, took an early lead at the finish with a time of 40:29. The next Soviet skier to reach the finish, start number 15 " [:a {:href "/athletes/83088"} "Radiya Yeroshina"] ", ended her race in excellent style with 38:16, over two minutes faster than the current leader. " [:a {:href "/athletes/81534"} "Alevtina Kolchina"] ", married to double bronze medalist " [:a {:href "/athletes/88115"} "Pavel Kolchin"] ", finished a few minutes later and was half a minute behind Yeroshina in second place, and the next to come was Kozyreva. The World Champion had to struggle hard to beat Yeroshina with a scant five second margin. From one of the latest starting numbers, the 25-year-old Swede " [:a {:href "/athletes/81003"} "Sonja Edström"] " was able to split the leading Soviet trio and secured a surprising bronze medal, only 12 seconds behind the Olympic Champion Kozyreva. Kozyreva won the first gold medal by a Soviet woman at the Olympics."] "\n"] [:button {:id "button265855", :class "btn btn-default"} "Details"] [:script {} "$('#button265855').click(splits)"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "32"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/80591"} "Lyubov Kozyreva"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "p